BAR Droid phone version of BAR's Idle Builders (luaui/widgets/gui_idle_builders.lua): not drawn and taking no presses
while the app's touch dock is up (WG.BarDroidPortrait.active()), whose groups strip shows the idle builders by type.
BAR places this box right of its Unit Groups (see phone-widget-gui_unitgroups.lua.patch, the same reason: on the
unfolded Fold7 sideways a sliver of the two showed at the split dock's right block whenever the dock's groups strip was
hidden, dev phone 2026-11-15). Its DrawScreen also runs its update; skipped meanwhile, it runs again once the dock is
gone (the pad: BAR's own screen back). Applied by the engine (BarDroidPhoneLuaDir) to BAR's file as LuaUI loads it; if
a block finds no place, BAR's own file runs. Both places are the same in every BAR release on the dev phone,
test-31465 to test-31958.

@@@ find
function widget:DrawScreen()
	gl.Blending(GL_SRC_ALPHA, GL_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA)
	if not spec or showWhenSpec then
@@@ with
function widget:DrawScreen()
	-- BAR Droid (phone): the touch dock up, its groups strip has the idle builders
	if WG.BarDroidPortrait and WG.BarDroidPortrait.active and WG.BarDroidPortrait.active() then
		return
	end
	gl.Blending(GL_SRC_ALPHA, GL_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA)
	if not spec or showWhenSpec then
@@@ end

@@@ find
function widget:MousePress(x, y, button)
	if Spring.IsGUIHidden() then
		return
	end
@@@ with
function widget:MousePress(x, y, button)
	if Spring.IsGUIHidden() then
		return
	end
	-- BAR Droid (phone): not drawn while the touch dock is up, so no presses either
	if WG.BarDroidPortrait and WG.BarDroidPortrait.active and WG.BarDroidPortrait.active() then
		return
	end
@@@ end
